                  <msItem>
                     <title>Sermones I. Ianuensis</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">On Westcote, see BRUO, pp. 2021-22, noting that
                        he died in June 1418 and that his gift must date from 1417/18, not a century
                        earlier as the transcription above suggests.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Bernard, Catalogi (1697), no. 2096.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Medieval binding of white leather over rounded
                        boards.</note>
                     <msItem>
                        <title>1. Sermones dominicales fratris Jacobi ordinis fratruum perdicatorum
                           archiepiscopi Januensis super euuangelia per circulum anni (incipit:
                           Humane labilis vite . . .; medieval foliation: fol. I-CCLIX).</title>
                     </msItem>
                     <msItem>
                        <title>2. Sermones festiuales per circulum anni fratris Iacobi (incipit:
                           Vestigia eius . . .; pagination: pp. I-CCLXXXV).</title>
                     </msItem>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
